sw-global-war-supply-work-title = Work: supply delivery
sw-global-war-supply-work-carrier = Your held or pulled container
sw-global-war-supply-work-select-carrier = Explicitly select a transfer container
sw-global-war-supply-work-help = Claim published cargo. At the source, hold a suitable container in your active hand or pull a crate and load the items: an open crate closes when loaded. Bring the same container to the receiving point, keep a crate shut, and submit it. Each delivery needs no minister approval. The task grants no general warehouse or budget access.
sw-global-war-supply-work-select-delivery = Select published cargo
sw-global-war-supply-work-select-work = Select a task
sw-global-war-supply-work-delivery = Order #{ $number }. { $item }: { $count } available.
sw-global-war-supply-work-row = Order #{ $number }. { $item }: { $count }. Worker: { $worker }
sw-global-war-supply-work-route = Order #{ $number }. Source: { $sourceName }, { $source }. Receiving point: { $recipientName }, { $recipient }. { $status }
sw-global-war-supply-work-details = Order #{ $number }. Assigned: { $item }, { $count }. Source: { $sourceName }, { $source }. Receiving point: { $recipientName }, { $recipient }. { $requirements } { $status }
sw-global-war-supply-work-at-source = Cargo is waiting at the source. You may claim part of the available quantity; one task can be active at a time.
sw-global-war-supply-work-recover = This cargo is already in the container you are holding or pulling. Its previous work authority was released; a new task allows delivery of the actual cargo without another purchase.
sw-global-war-supply-work-claim = Claim the entered quantity
sw-global-war-supply-work-collect = Load the selected container
sw-global-war-supply-work-accept = Submit cargo from the selected container
sw-global-war-supply-work-release = Release work authority; keep order and cargo
sw-global-war-supply-work-revoke = Revoke work authority; keep order and cargo
sw-global-war-supply-work-head = Revoke as an explicit head decision
sw-global-war-supply-work-head-notice = The head made an explicit decision on a delivery task. The decision was journaled.
sw-global-war-supply-work-success = Action completed. The current task state is shown below.
sw-global-war-supply-work-transfer-failed = Transfer failed. Approach the required point, hold the same suitable container in your active hand or pull it, and check access, available space (a crate holds up to 30 items), and all assigned items: an open crate spills its cargo, so close it with the items inside. No partial payment was made.
sw-global-war-supply-work-assigned = Authority granted. Assigned items await collection at the source.
sw-global-war-supply-work-collected = Items are in the container. Deliver it to the receiving point.
sw-global-war-supply-work-completed = Assigned items were actually accepted. Payment cannot be repeated.
sw-global-war-supply-work-released = Work authority released. The state order remains and cargo was not moved. The next worker must hold the container in their active hand or pull it and claim its published delivery.
sw-global-war-supply-work-revoked = Work authority was revoked or the appointment became invalid. New actions are denied; cancelling the state order is separate. The actual container was not moved. A current worker holds that same container in their active hand or pulls it, selects its published remainder, and claims a new delivery task.
sw-global-war-supply-source-point = Supply store #{ $number }: { $name }
sw-global-war-supply-arsenal-point = Arsenal #{ $number }: { $name }
sw-global-war-supply-work-point-lost = Unavailable former point
sw-global-war-supply-failure-workbusy = You already have an active task. Complete it or explicitly release its work authority.
sw-global-war-supply-failure-quantitychanged = The available quantity changed: some cargo was assigned or became unavailable. Review the remainder and explicitly choose a quantity again.
sw-global-war-supply-failure-invalidquantity = Quantity must be a whole number from 1 to 120.
sw-global-war-supply-work-quantity-remaining = { $count } available. Your input was preserved; change it for a new attempt.
sw-global-war-supply-work-require-magazine = Acceptance requires the assigned compatible functional magazine. Charge is tracked separately and is not promised by this delivery.
sw-global-war-supply-work-require-medicine = Acceptance checks the specified full contents of every assigned medical item.
sw-global-war-supply-work-require-ration = Acceptance requires the complete assigned ration with all contents and a full flask.
sw-global-war-supply-work-require-equipment = Acceptance checks the assigned suitable standard item; a different item cannot replace it.
